1
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:17,500
Those who ceaselessly hone the art
of killing are known as masters.

2
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:22,157
These lethal abilities, dutifully
passed down through many generations,

3
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,200
have become what are
called modified bloodlines.

4
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:28,837
This is the story of one such master,

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,720
Hikaru Gero of the Poison Clan
and his greatest challenge yet,

6
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,180
to get married.

7
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:00,960
What's that love?

8
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,257
Fun, fun, fun, you're so cool.

9
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,693
Oh, bah, bah, bah, bah!

10
00:01:23,506 --> 00:01:24,336
So sick.

11
00:01:25,332 --> 00:01:26,162
So sick.

12
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,360
Kill or kiss?

13
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,977
Let's go!

14
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,420
Kill or kiss.

15
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:11,257
She's the real head of the Beast Clan?

16
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,820
Then that means Toshiro is... Well done.

17
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:15,728
But I'll take it from here.

18
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,660
I assume you won't object.

19
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:28,800
The two of you are such good
boys, knowing not to overstep.

20
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,900
It's the wild dogs who get put down.

21
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:40,680
By the way, Hikaru, based on what
I've heard, you're looking for a mate.

22
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:46,258
Something tells me you
wouldn't mind becoming my pet.

23
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:51,697
As the heads of our families,
no doubt we'll meet again.

24
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:52,880
Who knows?

25
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:56,569
Maybe the five great families
will move towards unification.

26
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,560
Well, guess we're done here. Huh?

27
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,080
You shift gears fast.

28
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,820
Just what all's left?

29
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,020
I mean, we saved Misadashiyama.

30
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:17,520
The Beast Clan's plot, it's
not happening now. Right.

31
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:18,740
You have a point.

32
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:21,277
Actually, the hard part.

33
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,460
That's up next.

34
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,231
The whole marriage thing.

35
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,860
You know, I'll root for you.

36
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,060
It'll work out.

37
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:33,850
Hey!

38
00:03:33,933 --> 00:03:34,763
Hikaru Gero!

39
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:42,120
Still in one piece? Somehow. We managed.

40
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:59,817
I want to thank all of you and now
you're gonna get the full taste of our

41
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:06,620
gratitude we prepared a little
something modified bloodline increments.

42
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:28,360
Little critters,
thanksgiving extravaganza!

43
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,860
Re-brand, girl, and become
the cuteness master!

44
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,320
Here it comes!

45
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:01,880
The big climax! Hit it!

46
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:07,260
Date!

47
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,484
We hope this expresses
just how grateful we are!

48
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:19,577
This whole ordeal taught
me a valuable lesson.

49
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:22,497
Small fry masters like
me can put on a nice

50
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:28,457
show and that's about it
but that's fine by me.

51
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:31,537
I'll still live with my head held up high

52
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:38,500
awesome really all of
you are cool as hell!

53
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,540
Sure are!

54
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:52,660
It was at that moment, world-class
marriage swindler, Mei Kinosaki,

55
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:55,508
built the spark between
Gero and Arashiyama.

56
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:58,789
We're not letting this
opportunity slip by.

57
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:03,360
Okay, who here saw last
week's Twisted Ropes?

58
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,620
Me, of course.

59
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:07,277
I didn't know you were also
a die-hard fan of ropes.

60
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,660
Now to steer this conversation.

61
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:14,197
Speaking of exciting dates, this one
time I went on a private jet ride.

62
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,237
Who are you seeing?

63
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,540
Oil baron.

64
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:21,192
Within minutes, I've expertly shifted
the conversation to love and romance.

65
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,440
Boring subject.

66
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:30,417
Oh, by the way, you haven't told us
what your girlfriend is like, Piichi.

67
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,912
She's the best there is.

68
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:38,357
Seeing her smile gives me the
courage to take on any job and

69
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:41,197
coming home to dinner with her
makes my exhaustion melt away.

70
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:45,017
When I have a day off spending
it with her gives me the strength

71
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:50,357
to handle the days after I
realize I'm not a decent person.

72
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:53,877
All of the normal happiness
humans feel that I'm

73
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:56,717
aiming for I learned
entirely from my girlfriend.

74
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:59,297
For as long as I live for?

75
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:02,086
For better or for worse,
she's the one for me.

76
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:07,980
In order to protect her,
I would do anything.

77
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:09,320
I mean it.

78
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:17,020
Pichi Nakagawa, you said that
without a hint of embarrassment!

79
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:19,610
Is this it?

80
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,640
The power of natural charm?

81
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:27,200
Look at Katsunova over
here. Wanna see a picture?

82
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:31,549
I didn't count on that, but it
certainly turned up the heat.

83
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:38,562
It's time we talked, because
Arashiyama's head over heels for you.

84
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,460
But her feelings?

85
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,700
They're also a double-edged sword.

86
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:49,912
Since she idolizes you, if the illusion
breaks, things could end like that.

87
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,620
This won't be like Ureshi no or Himekawa.

88
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:54,507
You need to be more careful.

89
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:58,391
Gato's grown a lot, so a pep
talk should get him pumped up.

90
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,220
You got it?

91
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:05,697
All you have to do is play
it cool like Piichi did,

92
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,309
and when the time's
right, get them digits.

93
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:11,479
Ready to introduce her to
the new and improved Gato?

94
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,900
Ah, we're almost back to shore.

95
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:17,721
Well, I guess this means goodbye.

96
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:21,247
Kinosaki-style courting
arts, bridge builder!

97
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:24,840
I'm sure gonna miss you and
your hammies, Arashiyama.

98
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:27,220
Yeah, me too. I bet.

99
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:29,640
That's your cue.

100
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,900
Make your move, Giddo!

101
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:35,520
I wanted to say...

102
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,980
You mean she likes me?

103
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,060
For real?

104
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,857
You're not pulling my leg?

105
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:49,440
Why would she like me?

106
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,860
Why would anyone like me?

107
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:54,160
Come on, focus!

108
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,541
Don't freeze up!

109
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,837
Is this because I told
him about her feelings?

110
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,940
Was it too soon?

111
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,560
Look at him!

112
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,564
He can't even construct a word!

113
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,193
He'll never get her number at this rate!

114
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:10,060
Hikaru-Gero, what's the matter with you?

115
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,376
Cat got your tongue?

116
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,860
Shoot, it's hopeless.

117
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,129
Better put out this fire and
try to salvage whatever's left.

118
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:25,220
How about I go first, then?

119
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,100
I like you!

120
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,520
Did someone say something?

121
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:46,500
I, uh, like you.

122
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,600
There's just one problem.

123
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:54,600
I can't be the one who marries you.

124
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,130
Huh?

125
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:59,489
I overheard you were
looking for a partner.

126
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,460
And thought maybe I had a shot.

127
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:04,280
But no.

128
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:06,800
This might sound dumb.

129
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,472
But I'm not good enough.

130
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,020
At least not yet.

131
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,357
I don't feel confident about my work.

132
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,381
And I'm an emotional train wreck.

133
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:23,420
Even if by some miracle I got you to accept
me, I'd be dependent on you. A burden.

134
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:24,897
Being dead weight.

135
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:27,039
That's the last thing I would want.

136
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:28,440
I'm sorry.

137
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:31,517
I know this is totally
half-assed and self-centered.

138
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,457
But I'm going to build myself up.

139
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,187
Until I'm crazy independent.

140
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:39,158
Then I'll confess my feelings again.

141
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,960
You saved my life!

142
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:42,330
Thank you!

143
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:44,538
I just did the job I was told to do.

144
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:50,397
Instead of being the same little girl who
idolized you, I'll become a strong woman.

145
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,245
The kind that can support you.

146
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,094
I'm gonna make you fall for me so hard!

147
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:56,740
You better be ready!

148
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:03,820
I bet I sound crazy!

149
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:05,058
Don't listen to me!

150
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,560
Too late for that.

151
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,202
I don't really know what to say.

152
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:15,148
Someone like you,
thinking so much about me.

153
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:22,160
Never once in my whole life has a
person said anything like that to me.

154
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,680
I'll wait for you.

155
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:37,830
Yeah, same.

156
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:44,660
Until then, would it be okay
if we exchanged numbers?

157
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:47,980
Sure, they're a perfect match!

158
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:49,040
Do it already!

159
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:54,840
Added, you're in my
contacts now. Same for you.

160
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:58,275
Well, at least they're hitting it off.

161
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,640
I'm aiming to form the perfect marriage.

162
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,200
For both of them.

163
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,357
Send my fee with the extra
charges to the designated account.

164
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,857
If you miss the payment
deadline, I'll kill you!

165
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:14,920
Bye-bye!

166
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:17,760
Did she seem mad?

167
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:20,380
When did Piichi leave?

168
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,599
He was right here.

169
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,997
Welcome back, honey bunches.

170
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,668
It's good to be back, Mary.

171
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,060
How did it go?

172
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:34,120
It's just, group activities
aren't your thing.

173
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:38,809
So an overnight on an island with a
bunch of strangers sounds a little rough.

174
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:43,737
Well, yeah, it was kind of
weird at first, I guess.

175
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:47,300
But I got along pretty
okay with those guys.

176
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:49,180
Well, is that so?

177
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:52,717
In that case, sounds like you
ended up making new friends.

178
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:53,940
Hold on a sec.

179
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:55,880
Do you think so?

180
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:01,760
Oh, also, I learned how to
prep and cook a giant squid.

181
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,942
How do you feel about ink pasta?

182
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:05,720
I love it.

183
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,998
We should add it to the cafe's menu.

184
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,230
Yeah.

185
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,140
So what's next for you, Arashiyama?

186
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,100
Well, I'm glad you asked.

187
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:20,077
I'm going into business and
starting my own detective agency.

188
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:24,940
Not the entertainment industry
after that show you put on for us?

189
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,240
It was incredible.

190
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:30,488
Being a detective is
so much cooler, though.

191
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:35,865
Besides, I want to find out where
my big brother disappeared to.

192
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:38,360
Meow, meow!

193
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,280
See you around!

194
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,790
Arashiyama.

195
00:13:45,873 --> 00:13:48,180
She's great, but she's not the only one.

196
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,660
Himekawa, Ureshino too.

197
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:56,159
They're all beyond amazing, and
they've all been putting the work in.

198
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:59,920
I need to do the same
and be way more charming.

199
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:04,480
I'll be a man who's worthy of their love!

200
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:13,317
Then I'll whip you into shape with my
patented training of a thousand doormans!

201
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,360
Please do.

202
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,000
Good evening, Tadawaki.

203
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,620
How's our new poison vat treating you?

204
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,360
Is it everything you hoped for?

205
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:50,392
I nearly died and I've never been better!

206
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,980
So, teacher, what can I do for you?

207
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:58,220
It's concerning Master Hikaru's marriage.

208
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:01,800
Tell me more.

209
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:09,869
I've got good vibes
from all three of them.

210
00:15:10,260 --> 00:15:11,517
There's my boss at work.

211
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,537
A guy my age from a different school.

212
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:16,679
And an underclassman I met
at a club in junior high.

213
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,957
There's no way I could
pick only one of them.

214
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,511
Seeing as how I love each of them to bits.

215
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,500
Help me out, advisor.

216
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,120
What should I do?

217
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:29,120
I see your problem

218
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:33,037
Um, now all three of them want to
take me out on a date for my birthday.

219
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,000
Oh, really?

220
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:35,050
But you know...

221
00:15:35,133 --> 00:15:36,340
Romantic counseling?

222
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:37,990
Yep.

223
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:42,700
May the love evangelist, followers
only, kiss your worries goodbye.

224
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:49,217
Next time while I'm doing my side hustle,
I want you to sit in on the sessions.

225
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,800
Why would I ever...

226
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,000
Is this it?

227
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,660
My practice to max my charm?

228
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:58,800
It went over Himekawa,
Ureshino, and Arashiyama?

229
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,440
The training of a thousand torments!

230
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,597
I've endured a hundred already.

231
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:05,033
Only nine hundred left.

232
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:08,360
I say bring it on!

233
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,840
So what am I supposed to do now?

234
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:15,140
Well, this is just a suggestion.

235
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:19,097
But why don't you triple book so you
can hang out with all three of them?

236
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,740
I never thought of that.

237
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,640
Thanks a bunch!

238
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:24,920
Good luck!

239
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,350
Hi there, you.

240
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:27,900
So about my birthday.

241
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:32,060
Please let that be the toughest one. Yo!

242
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,794
Before school ends, I've gotta
ask out the team manager!

243
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:38,920
Only all the other players like her too!

244
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,797
But no one's feelings for
her are stronger than mine!

245
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:45,280
How do I score the final
try and win over her heart?

246
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:47,249
You should build this one.

247
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:59,380
For starters, be yourself
around her. What else?

248
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:01,360
Be polite. Got it!

249
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,080
Thanks, coach!

250
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:04,680
Good luck!

251
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:06,170
Hmm!

252
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:08,920
Break time.

253
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,117
The bathroom's sparkling clean! Who?

254
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,520
Is it a magic trick?

255
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,380
Was my advice good enough?

256
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,820
Okay, break's done.

257
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,040
Now back to work.

258
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:31,960
At first, I only saw it as a fling,
but now it feels so much more real.

259
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:38,257
Ever since graduating from college,
I've been swamped with work.

260
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:40,440
I haven't met any nice girls.

261
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:46,864
For quite a long time i've been
teaching a spanish cooking class.

262
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:50,972
And one of my students has my
heart dancing a paso double.

263
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:58,491
Yeah what do you think any feedback on
my song i wrote it for my sweetheart?

264
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:04,355
I'm wondering whether i should ask
out this girl we're in the same year.

265
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:08,300
I met an older woman on a trip
i can't get her out of my head.

266
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,220
Five years now under the same roof.

267
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,360
Where's my ring?

268
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,577
I'm madly in love with my
Spanish cooking teacher.

269
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:19,860
Things are spicy.

270
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,560
We can fit in another 20 today, right?

271
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:28,260
I've got no choice.

272
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:30,020
It's my only hope.

273
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:34,580
Intellectual linguistic
enhancer toxin. Silver tongue!

274
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:36,457
Whoa, stop that!

275
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:39,128
Kill yourself just to
get out of counseling!

276
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:42,660
Admit it, I'm hopeless. I know.

277
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,393
Everybody is fighting their own battles.

278
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:50,477
How can I possibly give them the
answers they desperately need?

279
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,000
You're doing just fine.

280
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:56,297
Everyone has to work as hard as you.

281
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:58,615
I just wanted you to see for yourself.

282
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,140
Honestly, there are no right answers.

283
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,765
Everyone's doing their best in
figuring out their own situation.

284
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,138
Deciding what's best for themselves.

285
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:13,660
Do you remember the other day?

286
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:19,260
When Arashiyama said she liked you, it
was like you lost all your confidence.

287
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:24,778
Your expression said, I can't accept
her feelings the way I'd like to.

288
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:31,037
But you see, that just proves
you're like everyone else.

289
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:34,238
And you're giving your love
life all you've got, too.

290
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:35,840
Baby steps.

291
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,440
Don't give up.

292
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,801
Because you're on the right path.

293
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:44,557
Don't get me wrong, though.

294
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,522
You still have a long way to go.

295
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:50,980
Thank you very much.

296
00:19:53,180 --> 00:19:54,460
One sec. Huh?

297
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:56,350
Huh?

298
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,380
Best of luck out there.

299
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:03,570
Same.

300
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:08,400
Why the candy kit?

301
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,080
I'm rewarding myself.

302
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:11,610
What?

303
00:20:11,693 --> 00:20:14,900
Let's really celebrate
with sukiyaki! Sorry.

304
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:18,120
I've actually got plans.

305
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,180
How about a rain check?

306
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:25,831
Fine, but you owe me fancy sukiyaki and
sushi for the after party, got that?

307
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,900
Kinosaki. Hmm?

308
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:33,700
I want to say, even since the first
day I met you strapped to that chair,

309
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:37,920
and you agreed to help me by
becoming my marriage advisor,

310
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,264
we've been through a whole lot.

311
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:44,100
And, well, the truth is,

312
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:48,700
no matter what we dealt with, I
had a great time through all of it.

313
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:54,537
I mean, before I met you, the best
thing I had going for me was this.

314
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:56,020
DIY candy kits.

315
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,580
What I'm saying is.

316
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:01,137
I hope you'll continue guiding me.

317
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,180
in my search for a bride.

318
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:07,930
Ghetto.

319
00:21:10,380 --> 00:21:11,780
Just leave it to me.

320
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:13,569
I'll make sure it happens.

321
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:15,617
You're going to end up happily married.

322
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:16,800
I guarantee it.

323
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,880
Hikaru it's been way too long

324
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:38,935
Thanks for making time for me tonight?

325
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,680
So how's the search?

326
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:44,020
Pretty okay, I guess What?

327
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,711
You mean it's going well?

328
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,577
That advisor must be a miracle worker.

329
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:50,080
You could have a little more faith in me!

330
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,580
Still, you might have to hurry.

331
00:21:56,860 --> 00:21:59,900
There's a rumor about the
ghetto branch families.

332
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:01,890
Dark.

333
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,460
He's up to something.

334
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:27,100
Here I go.

335
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:28,450
Ada.

336
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:37,930
ga.

337
00:22:38,013 --> 00:22:38,843
Try. ERS. Ga.

338
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,410
Minute.

339
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:13,380
Bye bye. Bye bye.

340
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,560
Love me.
